/P 261 0 R
/E (Finally, the U.S. military should closely train with federal agencies and departments, as well as law enforcement. This would baseline understanding of the threat of drones in the homeland and shape interoperability for counter-drone operations, which will help protect Americans at events such as the World Cup. This will unfold across the U.S. from June to July 2026. Training opportunities exist at the Joint Counter-Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems University in Oklahoma, which is designed to enhance miliary readiness to confront drones. Similarly, the Federal Bureau of Investigation recently opened a National Counter-Unmanned Training Center in Alabama that also enables joint training. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12 486 0 R 14 487 0 R 16]
